  "label": "audience description",
  "description": "The intended audience is individuals who are familiar with or find humor in racialized stereotypes, particularly anti-Black stereotypes such as the 'watermelon and fried chicken' food stereotype. The meme targets viewers who may not recognize the harmfulness of mocking a Black woman’s food preference, or who may be conditioned to find such racialized humor amusing. The audience is likely to be those who do not identify with the targeted community (Black people) or who hold implicit biases that make them receptive to the meme’s offensive punchline.",
